      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl lg:text-3xl text-ink mb-4">Skirting and architrave across West Yorkshire</h2>
      <p class="text-ink/70 mb-3">
        Heritage Joiners fits <a href="/services/skirting-architrave" class="text-oak underline">skirting board and architrave</a> across Pontefract, Wakefield and the wider West Yorkshire area, as part of <a href="/services/second-fix-carpentry" class="text-oak underline">second fix carpentry</a> or on its own.
      </p>
      <p class="text-ink/70 mb-3">
        Related reading: <a href="/guides/standard-door-sizes" class="text-oak underline">standard door sizes</a> covers the linings these architraves finish against, <a href="/services/doors" class="text-oak underline">door hanging</a> covers the doors that hang in them, and <a href="/services/timber-repair" class="text-oak underline">timber repair</a> covers making good where old mouldings have been damaged.
      </p>
      <p class="text-ink/70">
        For period work where an existing profile has to be matched, see <a href="/repair-or-replace" class="text-oak underline">the repair-or-replace framework</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-bone">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-ink mb-4">Trying to match an existing moulding?</h2>
      <p class="text-ink/70 mb-8 mx-auto">
        Send a photograph of the cut end, square-on with a rule alongside it, and the overall height and thickness. That is usually enough for an honest first view on whether it can be matched off the shelf or wants running bespoke.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <WhatsAppCTA message="Hi Heritage Joiners, I'd like help matching a moulding profile" />
        <PhoneLink phone={phone.tel} display={phone.display} variant="secondary" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
